/-!
# The finite group of signed monomials of a Clifford algebra

Let `b` be an orthogonal basis of a quadratic module `(M, Q)` whose generators square to `±1`, that
is `Q (b i) = 1` or `Q (b i) = -1` for every index `i`; over `ℂ` this is a normalized orthogonal
basis `e_i² = 1` of `ℂⁿ`. The subgroup `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q b` of the units of
`CliffordAlgebra Q` generated by `-1` and the generators `ι Q (b i)` is the group

`G = {±e_s : s a finite set of indices}`,

where `e_s = ι Q (b i₁) * ⋯ * ι Q (b iₖ)` for `s = {i₁ < ⋯ < iₖ}` is the basis vector
`CliffordAlgebra.basis Q b s`. Its multiplication is the sign rule
`CliffordAlgebra.basis_mul_basis`: `e_s * e_t = ±e_{s ∆ t}`. Its element `ε = -1` is central.
When the ring is nontrivial, `2` is invertible, and the finite index type has `n` elements,
the group is finite of order `2 ^ (n + 1)`.

That central element generates the **sign subgroup** `⟨ε⟩`, which is normal because it is central.
Every counting claim about it below assumes a nontrivial coefficient ring in which `2` is
invertible; in characteristic two `ε = 1` and the sign subgroup is trivial. Under those hypotheses
`⟨ε⟩ = {1, ε}` has order two. Quotienting by it forgets the sign of a signed monomial. The quotient
is **commutative, with every element of order dividing two**: two signed monomials commute or
anticommute, so their commutator is `1` or `ε`, and the square of a signed monomial is `±1`. For a
finite orthogonal basis of `n` generators squaring to `±1` over such a ring the quotient has `2 ^ n`
elements, one for each index set `s`, and the characters of `G` that kill `ε` are exactly the
characters of the quotient.

The group is a model of the Clifford algebra: the `e_s` form a basis of `CliffordAlgebra Q` and
multiply as the elements of `G` do, so the group algebra `R[G]` modulo the central element `ε + 1`
is the Clifford algebra. Sending each group element to its value gives an algebra map
`R[G] → CliffordAlgebra Q`. It is onto, since the generators lie in its image, and its kernel is
generated by `ε + 1`: every group element is `u` or `ε * u` for the element `u` of value `e_s`,
so modulo `ε + 1` every element of `R[G]` is a combination of these `u`, on which the map is
injective. Consequently an algebra map from the Clifford algebra to any `R`-algebra `A` is the same
as a monoid map `G → A` sending `ε` to `-1`; for `A = Module.End R W` this says that Clifford
modules are the representations of `G` in which `ε` acts by `-1`.

## Main definitions

* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q v`: the subgroup of `(CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ` generated by `-1`
  and the units whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)`, for any family `v` of vectors.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupEpsilon`: the central element `ε = -1`, named.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSign`: the central subgroup `⟨ε⟩` it generates.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv`: the characters killing `ε` are the characters of
  the quotient by `⟨ε⟩`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom Q v`: the algebra map from the group algebra of the group
  to the Clifford algebra, sending each group element to its value.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv`: **the Clifford algebra as the group algebra
  modulo `ε + 1`**.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift`: algebra maps from the Clifford algebra are the monoid maps
  from the group sending `ε` to `-1`.

## Main results

* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroup_iff`: **the normal form**: a unit lies in the group exactly
  when its value is `e_s` or `-e_s` for some finite index set `s`.
* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_center_monomialGroup_iff`: a signed basis monomial is central exactly when
  its support is empty or is the full odd-cardinality index set.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg`: signed monomials commute or anticommute.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup_val_eq_or_neg_of_isConj`: conjugation changes a signed monomial by
  at most its central sign.
* `CliffordAlgebra.neg_one_mem_center_monomialGroup`: `ε = -1` is central.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_monomialGroup`: **the order** is `2 ^ (n + 1)` over a nontrivial
  ring in which `2` is invertible, and `CliffordAlgebra.finite_monomialGroup` is the finiteness
  that follows.
* `CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroupSign_iff`: the sign subgroup is `{1, ε}`, and
  `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_monomialGroupSign`: it has order two over a nontrivial ring in which
  `2` is invertible.
* `CliffordAlgebra.commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign`,
  `CliffordAlgebra.isMulCommutative_quotient_monomialGroupSign` and
  `CliffordAlgebra.exponent_quotient_monomialGroupSign_dvd_two`: the quotient by the sign subgroup
  is commutative of exponent dividing two.
* `CliffordAlgebra.natCard_quotient_monomialGroupSign`: that quotient has `2 ^ n` elements, again
  over a nontrivial ring in which `2` is invertible.
* `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective`: the group algebra maps onto the Clifford
  algebra whenever the vectors span and their squares are units.
* `CliffordAlgebra.ker_monomialGroupAlgHom`: for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to
  `±1`, the kernel of that map is the ideal generated by `ε + 1`.

## References

* H. B. Lawson and M.-L. Michelsohn, *Spin Geometry* (1989), Chapter I, §1.
-/

public section

open scoped symmDiff

namespace CliffordAlgebra

variable {R M I : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (Q : QuadraticForm R M)

/-- The **group of signed monomials** of a family `v` of vectors: the subgroup of the units of
`CliffordAlgebra Q` generated by `-1` and the units whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)`.

For a finite orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1` it is the finite group of the `±e_s`
(`CliffordAlgebra.mem_monomialGroup_iff`). -/
def monomialGroup (v : I → M) : Subgroup (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ :=
  Subgroup.closure {u | (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨ ∃ i, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)}

variable {Q} (v : I → M)

/-- The defining generators of the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem monomialGroup_def :
    monomialGroup Q v = Subgroup.closure {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ |
      (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨ ∃ i, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)} :=
  (rfl)

/-- The element `ε = -1` lies in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem neg_one_mem_monomialGroup : -1 ∈ monomialGroup Q v :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl (by simp))

/-- A unit whose value is a generator `ι Q (v i)` lies in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} {i : I}
    (h : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)) : u ∈ monomialGroup Q v :=
  Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨i, h⟩)

/-- A generator `ι Q (v i)` with `Q (v i)` a unit is the value of an element of the group of signed
monomials. -/
theorem exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι {i : I} (h : IsUnit (Q (v i))) :
    ∃ g : monomialGroup Q v, ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i) := by
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := isUnit_ι_of_isUnit Q h
  exact ⟨⟨w, mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι v hw⟩, hw⟩

/-- **The element `ε = -1` is central** in the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem neg_one_mem_center_monomialGroup :
    (⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ : monomialGroup Q v) ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q v) :=
  Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun _ ↦ Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp))

/-! ### The central element `ε` and the sign subgroup it generates -/

variable (Q) in
/-- **The central element `ε = -1`** of the group of signed monomials. The construction of the
group above spells this element out as `⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩`; the sign subgroup and
the quotient statements below are phrased with this name instead. -/
def monomialGroupEpsilon : monomialGroup Q v :=
  ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩

variable (Q) in
/-- **The sign subgroup `⟨ε⟩`** of the group of signed monomials: the central subgroup generated by
`ε = -1`. Quotienting by it forgets the sign of a signed monomial. -/
def monomialGroupSign : Subgroup (monomialGroup Q v) :=
  Subgroup.zpowers (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v)

@[simp]
theorem coe_monomialGroupEpsilon :
    (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = -1 :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v * monomialGroupEpsilon Q v = 1 :=
  Subtype.ext (by simp)

theorem monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign :
    monomialGroupEpsilon Q v ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v :=
  Subgroup.mem_zpowers _

/-- **The sign subgroup is `{1, ε}`**: `ε` squares to `1`, so its powers are itself and the
identity. -/
theorem mem_monomialGroupSign_iff {u : monomialGroup Q v} :
    u ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v ↔ u = 1 ∨ u = monomialGroupEpsilon Q v := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [monomialGroupSign, Subgroup.mem_zpowers_iff]
    rintro ⟨k, rfl⟩
    rcases Int.even_or_odd k with ⟨m, rfl⟩ | ⟨m, rfl⟩
    · exact Or.inl (by
        rw [← two_mul, zpow_mul, zpow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self, one_zpow])
    · exact Or.inr (by
        rw [zpow_add_one, zpow_mul, zpow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self, one_zpow, one_mul])
  · rintro (rfl | rfl)
    · exact one_mem _
    · exact monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign v

instance monomialGroupSign_normal : (monomialGroupSign Q v).Normal :=
  Subgroup.normal_of_le_center (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr (neg_one_mem_center_monomialGroup v))

/-- **The sign subgroup has order two** over a nontrivial coefficient ring in which `2` is
invertible: `ε` squares to `1`, and it is not `1` because the scalars of the Clifford algebra are a
faithful copy of `R` (`CliffordAlgebra.algebraMap_injective`), in which `1 ≠ -1`. -/
theorem natCard_monomialGroupSign [Nontrivial R] [Invertible (2 : R)] :
    Nat.card (monomialGroupSign Q v) = 2 := by
  have hne : monomialGroupEpsilon Q v ≠ 1 := by
    intro h
    have h1 : (-1 : CliffordAlgebra Q) = 1 := by
      simpa using congrArg (fun g : monomialGroup Q v ↦
        ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)) h
    have h2 : (-1 : R) = 1 := algebraMap_injective Q (by simp [h1])
    exact Invertible.ne_zero (2 : R) (by linear_combination -h2)
  rw [monomialGroupSign, Nat.card_zpowers]
  exact orderOf_eq_prime (by rw [pow_two, monomialGroupEpsilon_mul_self]) hne

/-! ### Commutation and conjugation of signed monomials -/

/-- Any two signed monomials commute or anticommute, without a normalization assumption on their
generator squares. -/
lemma monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    (c u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) u := by
  let S : Set (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ := {x | (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 ∨
    ∃ i, (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) = ι Q (v i)}
  have hgen : ∀ x ∈ S, ∀ y ∈ S, TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg x y := by
    intro x hx y hy
    dsimp [S] at hx hy
    rcases hx with hx | ⟨i, hx⟩ <;> rcases hy with hy | ⟨j, hy⟩
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
      apply Units.ext
      simp [hx, hy]
    · by_cases hij : i = j
      · subst j
        apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_commute
        apply Units.ext
        simp [hx, hy]
      · apply TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_semiconjBy
        apply Units.ext
        simpa [hx, hy] using ι_mul_ι_comm_of_isOrtho (hv i j hij)
  have hmonomial : monomialGroup Q v = Subgroup.closure S := by
    simpa only [S] using (monomialGroup_def (Q := Q) v)
  have hc : (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∈ Subgroup.closure S := by
    rw [← hmonomial]
    exact c.property
  have hu : (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∈ Subgroup.closure S := by
    rw [← hmonomial]
    exact u.property
  exact TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.of_mem_closure hgen hc hu

/-- Every conjugate of a signed Clifford monomial is itself or its negative. -/
lemma monomialGroup_val_eq_or_neg_of_isConj
    (v : I → M) (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j))
    {u w : monomialGroup Q v} (h : IsConj u w) :
  (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∨
      (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = -(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := isConj_iff.mp h
  have hmul := congrArg (fun z : monomialGroup Q v => (z : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c) hc
  have hcv : (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * u = (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c := by
    simpa [mul_assoc] using hmul
  have hcu := monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv c u
  rcases TauCeti.CommuteOrNeg.out hcu with hcu | hcu
  · left
    have hcancel : (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c :=
      hcv.symm.trans hcu.eq
    exact mul_right_cancel_iff.mp hcancel
  · right
    have hcancel : (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (-(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)) * c := by
      calc
        (w : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * c = (c : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * u := hcv.symm
        _ = (-(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)) * c := hcu.eq
    exact mul_right_cancel_iff.mp hcancel

/-! ### The quotient by the sign subgroup -/

/-- **The commutator of two signed monomials lies in the sign subgroup.** Signed monomials of
pairwise orthogonal generators commute or anticommute, so their commutator is `1` or `ε`;
`CliffordAlgebra.commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign` is the subgroup form. -/
theorem inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) (c u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    (c * u)⁻¹ * (u * c) ∈ monomialGroupSign Q v := by
  rcases (monomialGroup_commuteOrNeg v hv c u).out with h | h
  · refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mpr (Or.inl ?_)
    rw [inv_mul_eq_one]
    exact Subtype.ext h.eq
  · refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mpr (Or.inr (Subtype.ext ?_))
    have hcu : ((c * u : monomialGroup Q v) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)
        = -((u * c : monomialGroup Q v) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
      simpa [neg_mul] using h.eq
    push_cast [hcu]
    simp

/-- **The commutator subgroup of the group of signed monomials lies in the sign subgroup**, which
is the subgroup form of `CliffordAlgebra.inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign`. -/
theorem commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) :
    commutator (monomialGroup Q v) ≤ monomialGroupSign Q v := by
  rw [commutator_def, Subgroup.commutator_le]
  intro c _ u _
  have hcomm : c * u * c⁻¹ * u⁻¹ = (u⁻¹ * c⁻¹)⁻¹ * (c⁻¹ * u⁻¹) := by group
  rw [commutatorElement_def, hcomm]
  exact inv_mul_mul_comm_mem_monomialGroupSign v hv u⁻¹ c⁻¹

/-- **The quotient of the group of signed monomials by its sign subgroup is commutative**, because
the commutator subgroup lies in the sign subgroup. -/
theorem isMulCommutative_quotient_monomialGroupSign
    (hv : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → Q.IsOrtho (v i) (v j)) :
    IsMulCommutative (monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) :=
  Subgroup.Normal.quotient_commutative_iff_commutator_le.mpr
    (commutator_monomialGroup_le_monomialGroupSign v hv)

/-- **The characters of the group of signed monomials that send `ε` to `1` are the characters of
the quotient by the sign subgroup.** A character kills `ε` exactly when it kills the subgroup `ε`
generates, so it factors through the quotient. The values are allowed in any group, so this covers
the characters with values in the units of a ring as well as the sign characters. -/
def monomialGroupSignCharEquiv {H : Type*} [Group H] :
    {χ : monomialGroup Q v →* H // χ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) = 1} ≃
      ((monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) →* H) where
  toFun χ := QuotientGroup.lift _ χ.1 fun u hu ↦ by
    rcases (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff v).mp hu with rfl | rfl
    · exact map_one _
    · exact χ.2
  invFun ψ := ⟨ψ.comp (QuotientGroup.mk' (monomialGroupSign Q v)), by
    have hε := (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff (N := monomialGroupSign Q v)
      (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v)).mpr (monomialGroupEpsilon_mem_monomialGroupSign v)
    simp [hε]⟩
  left_inv _ := Subtype.ext (MonoidHom.ext fun _ ↦ rfl)
  right_inv ψ := MonoidHom.ext fun x ↦ by
    induction x using QuotientGroup.induction_on with | H u => rfl

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv` sends a monoid map killing `ε` to the map of the
quotient taking the class of a group element to its value. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupSignCharEquiv_apply_mk {H : Type*} [Group H]
    (χ : {χ : monomialGroup Q v →* H // χ (monomialGroupEpsilon Q v) = 1})
    (u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    monomialGroupSignCharEquiv v χ (QuotientGroup.mk u) = χ.1 u :=
  (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupSignCharEquiv` sends a monoid map of the quotient
to its composite with the quotient map. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupSignCharEquiv_symm_apply_coe {H : Type*} [Group H]
    (ψ : (monomialGroup Q v ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q v) →* H) (u : monomialGroup Q v) :
    ((monomialGroupSignCharEquiv v).symm ψ).1 u = ψ (QuotientGroup.mk u) :=
  (rfl)

/-! ### The group algebra of the group of signed monomials -/

variable (Q) in
/-- The algebra map from the group algebra of the group of signed monomials to the Clifford
algebra, sending each group element to its value. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupAlgHom :
    MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q v) →ₐ[R] CliffordAlgebra Q :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift R (CliffordAlgebra Q) (monomialGroup Q v)
    ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q v).subtype)

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom` sends a group element to its value. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_of (g : monomialGroup Q v) :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) g) =
      ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift_of ..

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom` sends `r` times a group element to `r` times its
value. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_single (g : monomialGroup Q v) (r : R) :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v (MonoidAlgebra.single g r) =
      r • ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  MonoidAlgebra.lift_single ..

/-- The element `ε + 1` of the group algebra, for `ε = -1` the central element of the group of
signed monomials, lies in the kernel of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom`. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_of_neg_one_add_one_eq_zero :
    monomialGroupAlgHom Q v
      (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ + 1) = 0 := by
  simp

/-- The element `ε + 1` of the group algebra is central. -/
private theorem of_neg_one_add_one_mem_center :
    MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ + 1 ∈
      Set.center (MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q v)) :=
  Semigroup.mem_center_iff.mpr fun y ↦
    ((MonoidAlgebra.of_commute (fun g ↦
      ((Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (neg_one_mem_center_monomialGroup v) g).symm)) y).add_left
        (Commute.one_left y)).eq.symm

/-- Multiplying a group element `g` by `ε + 1` gives `ε * g + g`. -/
private theorem of_neg_one_mul_add_of (g : monomialGroup Q v) :
    MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ * g) + MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g =
      MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g *
        (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ + 1) := by
  rw [mul_add, mul_one, ← map_mul,
    Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (neg_one_mem_center_monomialGroup v) g]

/-- The left ideal generated by the central element `ε + 1` of the group algebra is two-sided. -/
instance isTwoSided_span_of_neg_one_add_one :
    (Ideal.span {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q v) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup v⟩ +
      1}).IsTwoSided :=
  Ideal.isTwoSided_span_of_subset_center
    (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (of_neg_one_add_one_mem_center v))

/-- **The group algebra maps onto the Clifford algebra** when the vectors `v` span `M` and the
generators `ι Q (v i)` are units, that is, when every `Q (v i)` is a unit. -/
theorem monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective (hv : Submodule.span R (Set.range v) = ⊤)
    (hQ : ∀ i, IsUnit (Q (v i))) : Function.Surjective (monomialGroupAlgHom Q v) := by
  rw [← AlgHom.range_eq_top, eq_top_iff, ← adjoin_range_ι, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
  -- The vectors whose generator lies in the range form a submodule containing every `v i`.
  have hle : Submodule.span R (Set.range v) ≤
      (Subalgebra.toSubmodule (monomialGroupAlgHom Q v).range).comap (ι Q) := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι v (hQ i)
    exact ⟨MonoidAlgebra.of R _ g, by simp [hg]⟩
  rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
  exact hle (hv ▸ Submodule.mem_top)

/-- A generator squaring to `±1` squares to a unit. -/
private theorem isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one (hQ : ∀ i, Q (v i) = 1 ∨ Q (v i) = -1) (i : I) :
    IsUnit (Q (v i)) := by
  rcases hQ i with h | h <;> simp [h]

variable [Invertible (2 : R)] [LinearOrder I] {b : Module.Basis I R M}

/-- **The normal form of the group of signed monomials**: for an orthogonal basis whose generators
square to `±1`, a unit lies in `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroup Q b` exactly when its value is
`e_s` or `-e_s` for a finite index set `s`. -/
theorem mem_monomialGroup_iff (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} :
    u ∈ monomialGroup Q b ↔
      ∃ s, (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨ (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s := by
  constructor
  · -- The signed monomials contain the generators and are closed under products and inverses.
    intro hu
    induction hu using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem u hu =>
      rcases hu with hu | ⟨i, hu⟩
      · exact ⟨∅, Or.inr (by rw [hu, basis_empty])⟩
      · exact ⟨{i}, Or.inl (by rw [hu, basis_singleton])⟩
    | one => exact ⟨∅, Or.inl (by rw [Units.val_one, basis_empty])⟩
    | mul u v _ _ hu hv =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hu
      obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hv
      refine ⟨s ∆ t, ?_⟩
      rw [Units.val_mul]
      rcases basis_mul_basis_eq_or hb hQ s t with h | h <;>
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> rcases ht with ht | ht <;>
        simp only [hs, ht, neg_mul, mul_neg, neg_neg, h, true_or, or_true]
    | inv u _ hu =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hu
      refine ⟨s, ?_⟩
      -- `u * u = ±1`, so `u⁻¹ = ±u`.
      have huu : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * u = 1 ∨ (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * u = -1 := by
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> simpa only [hs, neg_mul_neg] using basis_mul_self_eq_or hb hQ s
      rcases huu with h | h
      · rw [Units.inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right h]
        exact hs
      · have hneg : (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * -u = 1 := by rw [mul_neg, h, neg_neg]
        rw [Units.inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right hneg]
        rcases hs with hs | hs <;> rw [hs] <;> simp
  · -- Peel off the generators one at a time, starting from the least index.
    rintro ⟨s, hs⟩
    induction s using Finset.induction_on_min generalizing u with
    | empty =>
      rw [basis_empty] at hs
      rcases hs with hs | hs
      · rw [Units.val_eq_one.mp hs]
        exact one_mem _
      · exact Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl hs)
    | insert a s ha ih =>
      -- The generator of `a` squares to `Q (b a) = ±1`, so it is a unit.
      have hsq : Q (b a) * Q (b a) = 1 := by rcases hQ a with h | h <;> rw [h] <;> norm_num
      let : Invertible (Q (b a)) := ⟨Q (b a), hsq, hsq⟩
      let := invertibleιOfInvertible Q (b a)
      let g := unitOfInvertible (ι Q (b a))
      have hg : g ∈ monomialGroup Q b := mem_monomialGroup_of_val_eq_ι b rfl
      have hgu : g⁻¹ * u ∈ monomialGroup Q b := by
        refine ih ?_
        rw [basis_insert_of_forall_lt hb ha] at hs
        -- Mathlib's `unitOfInvertible` has value `ι Q (b a)` and inverse `⅟(ι Q (b a))`.
        simp only [g, unitOfInvertible, Units.inv_mk, Units.val_mul]
        rcases hs with hs | hs
        · exact Or.inl (by rw [hs, invOf_mul_cancel_left])
        · exact Or.inr (by rw [hs, mul_neg, invOf_mul_cancel_left])
      simpa using mul_mem hg hgu

/-- For an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, every basis vector `e_s` is the value
of an element of the group of signed monomials. -/
theorem exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (s : Finset I) :
    ∃ u : monomialGroup Q b, ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := isUnit_basis hb s fun i _ ↦ isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i
  exact ⟨⟨u, (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mpr ⟨s, Or.inl hu⟩⟩, hu⟩

/-- **The order of the group of signed monomials**: for an orthogonal basis over a nontrivial ring
in which `2` is invertible, indexed by a type with `n` elements and whose generators square to `±1`,
the group has `2 ^ (n + 1)` elements, the `±e_s` for the `2 ^ n` index sets `s`. -/
theorem natCard_monomialGroup [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b) = 2 ^ (Fintype.card I + 1) := by
  -- Parametrize the values of the group by a sign and an index set.
  let f : ℤˣ × Finset I → CliffordAlgebra Q := fun p ↦ ((p.1 : ℤ) : R) • basis Q b p.2
  have hsign (ε : ℤˣ) : ((ε : ℤ) : R) = 1 ∨ ((ε : ℤ) : R) = -1 := by
    rcases Int.units_eq_one_or ε with rfl | rfl <;> simp
  have hne : (1 : R) ≠ -1 := by
    intro h
    have h2 : (2 : R) = 0 := by linear_combination h
    exact Invertible.ne_zero 2 h2
  -- The parametrization is injective: the basis vectors are independent and `1 ≠ -1`.
  have hf : Function.Injective f := by
    rintro ⟨ε, s⟩ ⟨ε', t⟩ h
    have h' := congrArg (basis Q b).repr h
    simp only [f, map_smul, Module.Basis.repr_self, Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul, mul_one,
      Finsupp.single_eq_single_iff] at h'
    rcases h' with ⟨rfl, hε⟩ | ⟨h0, -⟩
    · refine Prod.ext ?_ rfl
      rcases Int.units_eq_one_or ε with rfl | rfl <;> rcases Int.units_eq_one_or ε' with rfl | rfl
      · rfl
      · exact (hne (by simpa using hε)).elim
      · exact (hne (by simpa using hε.symm)).elim
      · rfl
    · rcases hsign ε with h | h <;> rw [h] at h0 <;> simp at h0
  -- Its image is the set of values of the group, by the normal form.
  have hrange : Units.val '' (monomialGroup Q b : Set (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) = Set.range f := by
    ext x
    simp only [Set.mem_image, SetLike.mem_coe, Set.mem_range, Prod.exists]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨s, hs | hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp hu
      · exact ⟨1, s, by simp [f, hs]⟩
      · exact ⟨-1, s, by simp [f, hs]⟩
    · rintro ⟨ε, s, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ s
      rcases hsign ε with h | h
      · exact ⟨u, u.2, by simp [f, h, hu]⟩
      · exact ⟨-1 * u, mul_mem (neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b) u.2, by simp [f, h, hu]⟩
  have hcard : Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b) = Nat.card (ℤˣ × Finset I) := by
    rw [← SetLike.coe_sort_coe, ← Nat.card_image_of_injective Units.val_injective, hrange,
      Nat.card_range_of_injective hf]
  rw [hcard]
  simp only [Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_prod, Fintype.card_units_int,
    Fintype.card_finset, pow_succ, mul_comm]

/-- A signed basis monomial is central in the finite monomial subgroup exactly when its support is
empty, or when it is the full index set of odd cardinality, for an orthogonal basis whose vectors
square to `±1` over a nontrivial commutative ring in which `2` is invertible. -/
theorem mem_center_monomialGroup_iff [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    {u : monomialGroup Q b} :
    u ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b) ↔
      ∃ s : Finset I,
        ((↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
          (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) ∧
        (s = ∅ ∨ (s = Finset.univ ∧ Odd s.card)) := by
  have central_comm_of_value (hu : u ∈ Subgroup.center (monomialGroup Q b))
      (s : Finset I) (hs : (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = basis Q b s ∨
        (↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -basis Q b s) :
      ∀ i : I, basis Q b s * ι Q (b i) = ι Q (b i) * basis Q b s := by
    intro i
    have hi : IsUnit (Q (b i)) := isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι b hi
    have hc := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp hu g
    have hc' : (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * (g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) =
        (g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) * (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) := by
      simpa using congrArg Subtype.val hc.symm
    have hc'' := congrArg Units.val hc'
    rcases hs with hs | hs
    · simpa [hs, hg] using hc''
    · simpa [hs, hg] using hc''
  constructor
  · intro hu
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff (b := b) hb hQ).mp u.property
    exact ⟨s, hs, (basis_comm_ι_iff hb (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ) s).mp
      (central_comm_of_value hu s hs)⟩
  · rintro ⟨s, hs, hpar⟩
    have hcenter : basis Q b s ∈ Subalgebra.center R (CliffordAlgebra Q) := by
      rcases hpar with rfl | ⟨rfl, hodd⟩
      · rw [basis_empty]
        exact one_mem _
      · exact basis_univ_mem_center_of_odd_card hb (by simpa using hodd)
    have hcomm_basis (x : CliffordAlgebra Q) :
        x * basis Q b s = basis Q b s * x :=
      Subalgebra.mem_center_iff.mp hcenter x
    rw [Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
    intro g
    apply Subtype.ext
    apply Units.ext
    rcases hs with hs | hs
    · simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Units.val_mul, hs] using
        hcomm_basis ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)
    · simpa only [Subgroup.coe_mul, Units.val_mul, hs, mul_neg, neg_mul] using
        congrArg Neg.neg (hcomm_basis ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q))

/-- **The group of signed monomials of a finite orthogonal basis is finite.** -/
theorem finite_monomialGroup [Finite I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Finite (monomialGroup Q b) := by
  have : Fintype I := Fintype.ofFinite I
  have h : Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [natCard_monomialGroup hb hQ]
    positivity
  exact (Nat.card_ne_zero.mp h).2

/-! ### The quotient by the sign subgroup of an orthogonal basis -/

/-- **A signed monomial squares into the sign subgroup**: when the generators square to `±1`, so
does every basis monomial `e_s`. -/
theorem mul_self_mem_monomialGroupSign (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (u : monomialGroup Q b) :
    u * u ∈ monomialGroupSign Q b := by
  have hval : (((u * u : monomialGroup Q b) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = 1 ∨
      (((u * u : monomialGroup Q b) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = -1 := by
    obtain ⟨s, hs | hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp u.2
    · simpa [hs] using basis_mul_self_eq_or hb hQ s
    · simpa [hs, neg_mul_neg] using basis_mul_self_eq_or hb hQ s
  refine (mem_monomialGroupSign_iff b).mpr ?_
  rcases hval with h | h
  · exact Or.inl (Subtype.ext (Units.ext h))
  · exact Or.inr (Subtype.ext (Units.ext h))

/-- **The quotient by the sign subgroup has exponent dividing two.** -/
theorem exponent_quotient_monomialGroupSign_dvd_two
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Monoid.exponent (monomialGroup Q b ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q b) ∣ 2 := by
  refine Monoid.exponent_dvd_of_forall_pow_eq_one fun x ↦ ?_
  induction x using QuotientGroup.induction_on with | H u =>
  rw [pow_two, ← QuotientGroup.mk_mul, QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
  exact mul_self_mem_monomialGroupSign hb hQ u

/-- **The quotient by the sign subgroup has `2 ^ n` elements**, one for each of the `2 ^ n` index
sets: the group of signed monomials has `2 ^ (n + 1)` elements and the sign subgroup has two. -/
theorem natCard_quotient_monomialGroupSign [Fintype I] [Nontrivial R]
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    Nat.card (monomialGroup Q b ⧸ monomialGroupSign Q b) = 2 ^ Fintype.card I := by
  have h := (monomialGroupSign Q b).card_eq_card_quotient_mul_card_subgroup
  rw [natCard_monomialGroup hb hQ, natCard_monomialGroupSign, pow_succ] at h
  exact (Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right two_pos h).symm

/-! ### The Clifford algebra as a quotient of the group algebra -/

/-- **The kernel of the group algebra map is generated by `ε + 1`**: for an orthogonal basis whose
generators square to `±1`, an element of the group algebra of the group of signed monomials maps to
zero in the Clifford algebra exactly when it is a multiple of `ε + 1`, for `ε = -1`. -/
theorem ker_monomialGroupAlgHom (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    RingHom.ker (monomialGroupAlgHom Q b) =
      Ideal.span
        {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ + 1} := by
  set x := MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ + 1 with hx
  refine le_antisymm (fun y hy ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
    (monomialGroupAlgHom_of_neg_one_add_one_eq_zero b)))
  -- Every basis vector `e_s` is the value of a group element `u s`.
  choose u hu using exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_basis hb hQ
  -- Lifting `e_s` back to `u s` is a linear section of the group algebra map, modulo `ε + 1`.
  let ψ : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₗ[R] MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b) :=
    (basis Q b).constr R fun s ↦ MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (u s)
  have key (z : MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b)) :
      z - ψ (monomialGroupAlgHom Q b z) ∈ Ideal.span {x} := by
    induction z using MonoidAlgebra.induction_on with
    | of g =>
      obtain ⟨s, hs | hs⟩ := (mem_monomialGroup_iff hb hQ).mp g.2
      · obtain rfl : g = u s := Subtype.ext (Units.ext (hs.trans (hu s).symm))
        rw [monomialGroupAlgHom_of, hu, Module.Basis.constr_basis, sub_self]
        exact zero_mem _
      · -- Here `g = ε * u s`, and `of g + of (u s) = of (u s) * (ε + 1)`.
        have hg : g = ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ * u s :=
          Subtype.ext (Units.ext (by simp [hs, hu]))
        have hmem : MonoidAlgebra.of R _ (u s) * x ∈ Ideal.span {x} :=
          Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self x)
        convert hmem using 1
        rw [monomialGroupAlgHom_of, hs, map_neg, Module.Basis.constr_basis, sub_neg_eq_add, hg,
          of_neg_one_mul_add_of]
    | add y z hy hz => simpa [add_sub_add_comm] using add_mem hy hz
    | smul r y hy => simpa [smul_sub] using Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ r hy
  simpa [RingHom.mem_ker.mp hy] using key y

/-- **The Clifford algebra is the group algebra of the group of signed monomials modulo
`ε + 1`**: for an orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, the class of a group element
maps to its value. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) :
    (MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b) ⧸
      Ideal.span {MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ + 1})
      ≃ₐ[R] CliffordAlgebra Q :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq R (ker_monomialGroupAlgHom hb hQ).symm).trans
    (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (monomialGroupAlgHom_surjective b b.span_eq
      (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ)))

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv` sends the class of `z` to its image under
`CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgHom`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_mk (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) (z : MonoidAlgebra R (monomialGroup Q b)) :
    monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ z) =
      monomialGroupAlgHom Q b z := by
  simp [monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv]

/-- The inverse of `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv` sends the value of a group
element to its class. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_symm_apply_coe
    (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b) (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1)
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    (monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ).symm
        ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MonoidAlgebra.of R (monomialGroup Q b) g) := by
  rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq, monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_mk, monomialGroupAlgHom_of]

/-- The algebra map from the Clifford algebra induced by a monoid map from the group of signed
monomials sending `ε` to `-1`; it is `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift`. -/
private noncomputable def monomialGroupLiftAux (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ = -1}) :
    CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ (MonoidAlgebra.lift R A _ f) fun _ hz ↦
      RingHom.mem_ker.mp ((Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
        (by simp [RingHom.mem_ker, f.2]))) hz)).comp
    (monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv hb hQ).symm.toAlgHom

/-- `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ f` sends the value of `g` to `f g`. -/
private theorem monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ = -1})
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ f ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = f.1 g := by
  simp only [monomialGroupLiftAux, AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom,
    monomialGroupAlgebraQuotientEquiv_symm_apply_coe]
  exact MonoidAlgebra.lift_of ..

/-- **The universal property of the Clifford algebra in terms of its signed monomials**: for an
orthogonal basis whose generators square to `±1`, algebra maps from the Clifford algebra to an
`R`-algebra `A` are the same as monoid maps from the group of signed monomials to `A` sending
`ε = -1` to `-1`. For `A = Module.End R W` this identifies the Clifford module structures on `W`
with the representations of the group on `W` in which `ε` acts by `-1`. -/
noncomputable def monomialGroupLift (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A] :
    {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ = -1} ≃
      (CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A) where
  toFun := monomialGroupLiftAux hb hQ
  invFun F := ⟨(F : CliffordAlgebra Q →* A).comp
      ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q b).subtype), by simp⟩
  left_inv f := Subtype.ext <| MonoidHom.ext fun g ↦ monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ f g
  right_inv F := by
    refine hom_ext (b.ext fun i ↦ ?_)
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_monomialGroup_val_eq_ι b (isUnit_of_eq_one_or_neg_one b hQ i)
    have := monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ ⟨(F : CliffordAlgebra Q →* A).comp
      ((Units.coeHom (CliffordAlgebra Q)).comp (monomialGroup Q b).subtype), by simp⟩ g
    simpa [hg] using this

/-- The algebra map `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift hb hQ f` sends the value of each group
element `g` to `f g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupLift_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (f : {f : monomialGroup Q b →* A // f ⟨-1, neg_one_mem_monomialGroup b⟩ = -1})
    (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    monomialGroupLift hb hQ f ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) = f.1 g :=
  monomialGroupLiftAux_apply_coe hb hQ f g

/-- The monoid map attached by `CliffordAlgebra.monomialGroupLift` to an algebra map `F` from the
Clifford algebra is `F` applied to the values of the group elements. -/
@[simp]
theorem monomialGroupLift_symm_apply_coe (hb : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).IsOrthoᵢ b)
    (hQ : ∀ i, Q (b i) = 1 ∨ Q (b i) = -1) {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (F : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[R] A) (g : monomialGroup Q b) :
    ((monomialGroupLift hb hQ).symm F).1 g = F ((g : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  (rfl)

end CliffordAlgebra
